,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.2634904043106021,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.0022596343003375777,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":1.1,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.8075314522790242,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.24912845835143527,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.2162282976861349,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.22356753085007863,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.003510669758844065,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":26.8,"_gate_margins":-0.0021087202926363792,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":47.9,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.09414835115730309,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0009550117696170979,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":51.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004848603035030492,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.00654,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Conagra Brands, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a branded consumer packaged goods food company primarily in the United States. The company operates in four segments: Grocery & Snacks, Refrigerated & Frozen, International, and Foodservice. The Grocery & Snacks segment primarily offers shelf stable food products through various retail channels. The Refrigerated & Frozen segment provides temperature-controlled food products through various retail channels. The International segment offers food products in various temperature states through retail and foodservice channels outside of the United States. The Foodservice segment offers branded and customized food products, including meals, entrees, sauces, and various custom-manufactured culinary products packaged for restaurants and other foodservice establishments. The company sells its products under the Birds Eye, Duncan Hines, Healthy Choice, Marie Callender's, Reddi-wip, Slim Jim, and Angie's BOOMCHICKAPOP brands. Conagra Brands, Inc. was incorporated in 1919 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John P. Brase | CEO, President & Director | Age 57","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 17K people. Revenue per employee of $648K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $56K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["ConAgra Brands, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer defensive business with a $7.3B market cap on $11.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +22% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 25% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $979M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -19.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage runs at 5.8\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 9.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.5pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Defensive peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 46% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Consumer Defensive tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Conagra Brands (CAG) vs. The Competition Financial Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/conagra-brands-cag-vs-the-competition-financial-analysis.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793884551.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Conagra (NYSE:CAG) Pops Above A Key Line: Real Turnaround?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/conagra-nysecag-pops-above-a-key-line-real-turnaround","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793713500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Conagra Brands (NYSE:CAG) Steady Enough to Support Its Dividend?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/dividend/is-conagra-brands-nysecag-steady-enough-to-support-its-dividend","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793615220.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Conagra Brands Inc's Dividend Analysis","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/conagra-brands-incs-dividend-analysis-100403723.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793873043.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"3 Beaten-Down Food Stocks With High Dividend Yields. Which Payouts Are Safe?","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/3-beaten-down-food-stocks-201713000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793996558.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.414,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"5 High-Yield Dividend Stocks That Could Be Headed for a Dividend Cut","source":"247wallst.com","link":"https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/11/05/5-high-yield-dividend-stocks-that-could-be-headed-for-a-dividend-cut/","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793908105.0,"or